ter you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T18:43:24-08:00","id":1055937,"title":"","content":"It was something along the lines of: &quot;If you ever run into one that's got a chip on their shoulder and smell like a Summer bonfire, make friends. They've got something they want to kill too.&quot;<br /> <br /> You know what, it definily was from the Sabotour write up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:31:30-08:00","id":1056101,"title":"","content":"I do love Leviathans from Beast calling werewolves &quot;the sharks of the land, in the best possible way&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:41:10-08:00","id":1056281,"title":"","content":"Dusksage, that is a good one.<br /> <br /> Another of mine is the Hunt Club on Ashwood Abbey, roughly, &quot;Amateurs. They claim to seek the ultimate thrill, but they only take it so far.&quot; - Mostly because I could see the Abbey's stereotype of the Hunt Club being exactly the same.<br /> <br /> From Werewolf, I like Elodoth on Irraka: &quot;Damn it, where did she go?&quot;<br /> <br /> Since fan ones have come up, I remember a (Masquerade) bloodline of Sun-worshippers. The Sabbat stereotype given for them was, &quot;Sounds like a problem that will take care of itself.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T14:48:15-08:00","id":1056327,"title":"","content":"Vampire Second Edition has an embarrassment of good ones:<br /> <br /> <b>Daeva on Mekhet: </b>They call us shallow. We call them concave.<br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu on Mekhet: </b>They are the silence. We are the stage whisper.<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue on Nosferatu:</b> If fear is your only tool, then every problem starts screaming.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T22:17:16-08:00","id":1056487,"title":"","content":"Galateids on Ulgans: &quot;Ugh. They <i>leak.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:56:30-07:00","id":1077145,"title":"","content":"The Sin-Eaters' stereotypes on other templates contain some of my favourites.<br /> <br /> The Forgotten stereotype on mortals is quite good: &quot;Don't risk it. It's a mug's game, man.&quot;<br /> The Torn have another good take on mortals: &quot;Just stay behind me. Stay behind me, and don't look too hard. And please, shut the #*%@ up.&quot;<br /> However, the crown jewel of the set, and possibly the entire World of Darkness, is the Prey stereotype on Mages: &quot;That's cheating.&quot;<br /> <br /> Half of the stereotypes from the Court of Mirrors in Princess: The Hopeful are really good (I echo the above sentiment that PtH has a lot of good stereotypes), but their stereotype on themselves deserves an honourable mention: &quot;No, you're <i>not</i> the True Heir! <i>I</i> am!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","user":"RougeMephilesClone","date":". 04-12-2017, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13233-rougemephilesclone","name":"RougeMephilesClone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}